applyVectorField -- apply a vector field to a function or functions
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        g=applyVectorField(M,f)
        g=applyVectorField(V,f)
        L=applyVectorField(M,l)
        L=applyVectorField(V,l)
        J=applyVectorField(m,f)
        J=applyVectorField(m,I)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of vector fields
      * V, a *note vector: (Macaulay2Doc)Vector,, a column from a matrix of
        vector fields
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, to apply the first
        parameter to
      * l, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of RingElements to apply the
        first parameter to
      * m, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, of vector fields
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal of functions to apply
        the first parameter to
  * Outputs:
      * g, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of RingElements
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

Apply the vector field(s) represented by M, V, or m, to the second parameter,
that is, use the vector field(s) as differential operator(s).

When the first parameter is a *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, or a *note
Vector: (Macaulay2Doc)Vector,, then the return type matches the second
parameter. If that is a *note RingElement: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, then
there must only be 1 column in the matrix. When the second parameter is a *note
List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, l of *note RingElement: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,s,
then the returned *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, is formed by applying each
vector field in turn to the first entry of l, then each vector field to the
second entry of l, etc.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y,z];                     |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : A=matrix {{x},{y},{0}};          |
|                                      |
|             3      1                 |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : B=matrix {{0},{0},{z}};          |
|                                      |
|             3      1                 |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                  |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : f=x*y-z^2;                       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : applyVectorField(A,f)            |
|                                      |
|o5 = 2x*y                             |
|                                      |
|o5 : R                                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i6 : applyVectorField(A,{f,x*f})      |
|                                      |
|              2       2               |
|o6 = {2x*y, 3x y - x*z }              |
|                                      |
|o6 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : applyVectorField(A|B,{f,x*f})    |
|                                      |
|               2    2       2       2 |
|o7 = {2x*y, -2z , 3x y - x*z , -2x*z }|
|                                      |
|o7 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+



When the first parameter is a *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, then the
return type is an *note Ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,. Applying a *note Module:
(Macaulay2Doc)Module, to a *note RingElement: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement, gives
the *note Ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, generated by applying each generator to
the function. Applying a *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, to an *note Ideal:
(Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, I produces the *note Ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, generated
by applying every element of the module to every element of I; this is
generated by not only the functions formed by applying each generator of the
module to each generator of I (as might be computed by the (Matrix,List)
version of this function), but also I times the ideal of coefficients of the
generators of the module.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : applyVectorField(image A,f)                             |
|                                                             |
|o8 = ideal(2x*y)                                             |
|                                                             |
|o8 : Ideal of R                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : applyVectorField(image A,ideal (f))                     |
|                                                             |
|                    2     2                                  |
|o9 = ideal (x*y, y*z , x*z )                                 |
|                                                             |
|o9 : Ideal of R                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : trim(ideal(applyVectorField(A,f))+ideal(f)*minors(1,A))|
|                                                             |
|                     2     2                                 |
|o10 = ideal (x*y, y*z , x*z )                                |
|                                                             |
|o10 : Ideal of R                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

