commutator -- the commutator of a collection of vector fields
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N=commutator(M)
        n=commutator(m)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of vector fields
      * m, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, of vector fields
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, with columns containing the
        brackets of pairs of columns of M
      * n, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the module generated by
        brackets of elements of m

Description
===========

When given a *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, this returns a *note Matrix:
(Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, with columns containing the brackets of pairs of columns
of M.

When given a *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, this returns the *note
Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, generated by $[X,Y]$, for $X$ and $Y$ in the
module m. This is a superset of the module generated by the brackets of
generators of m; see *note bracket: bracket, for more details.

In either case, *note commutator: commutator, computes much the same thing as
calling *note bracket: bracket, with repeated parameters, but is more efficient
because it takes advantage of skew-symmetry.

See *note differences between certain bracketing functions: differences between
certain bracketing functions, for more information.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y];                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D=derlog(ideal (x*y*(x-y)))                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = image | x 0     |                                                       |
|           | y xy-y2 |                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|                             2                                               |
|o2 : R-module, submodule of R                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : commutator(gens D)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | 0     |                                                               |
|     | xy-y2 |                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             2      1                                                        |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : bracket(gens D,gens D)                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = | 0 0     0      0 |                                                    |
|     | 0 xy-y2 -xy+y2 0 |                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|             2      4                                                        |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : commutator(D)                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = image | 0     x2 0       0 0 xy 0      x2y-xy2 0            |           |
|           | xy-y2 xy x2y-xy2 0 0 y2 xy2-y3 xy2-y3  x2y2-2xy3+y4 |           |
|                                                                             |
|                             2                                               |
|o5 : R-module, submodule of R                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : bracket(D,D)                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = image | 0 0     0      0 x2 0       0 0 xy 0      x2y-xy2 0             |
|           | 0 xy-y2 -xy+y2 0 xy x2y-xy2 0 0 y2 xy2-y3 xy2-y3  x2y2-2xy3+y4  |
|                                                                             |
|                             2                                               |
|o6 : R-module, submodule of R                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x2 0       0 0 xy 0      x2y-xy2 0            |                              |
|xy x2y-xy2 0 0 y2 xy2-y3 xy2-y3  x2y2-2xy3+y4 |                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, and *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,
versions of this routine compute different things; see *note differences
between certain bracketing functions: differences between certain bracketing
functions,.

