derlog -- compute the logarithmic (tangent) vector fields to an ideal
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        m=derlog(I)
        m=derlog(f)
        n=derlogH(L)
        n=derlogH(f)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, nonempty, of RingElements
  * Outputs:
      * m, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the module of logarithmic
        vector fields for I or ideal(f)
      * n, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the module of vector fields
        that annihilates f or the entries of L

Description
===========

derlog computes the module of logarithmic vector fields to an affine variety
defined by I or f; these are the ambient vector fields tangent to the variety.

derlogH computes the module of ambient vector fields tangent to all level sets
of f or of the entries of L.

Note that derlog(I)=der(I,I) and derlogH(L)=der(L,0); see *note der: der,.



+------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y,z];             |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : f=x*y-z^2;               |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : derlog(ideal (f))        |
|                              |
|o3 = image | 2x 0  2z 0  |    |
|           | 0  2y 0  2z |    |
|           | z  z  y  x  |    |
|                              |
|                             3|
|o3 : R-module, submodule of R |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : derlogH(f)               |
|                              |
|o4 = image | x  2z 0  |       |
|           | -y 0  2z |       |
|           | 0  y  x  |       |
|                              |
|                             3|
|o4 : R-module, submodule of R |
+------------------------------+
|i5 : dH=derlogH({f})          |
|                              |
|o5 = image | x  2z 0  |       |
|           | -y 0  2z |       |
|           | 0  y  x  |       |
|                              |
|                             3|
|o5 : R-module, submodule of R |
+------------------------------+

Although every element of dH annihilates f, they do not annihilate the ideal
generated by f:

+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : applyVectorField(dH,f)                     |
|                                                |
|o6 = ideal (0, 0, 0)                            |
|                                                |
|o6 : Ideal of R                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : applyVectorField(dH,ideal(f))              |
|                                                |
|                     3     2      2   2       2 |
|o7 = ideal (x*y*z - z , x*y  - y*z , x y - x*z )|
|                                                |
|o7 : Ideal of R                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note VectorFields: Top, -- vector fields
  * *note der: der, -- compute the module of vector fields which send one set
    to another
  * *note isLogarithmic: isLogarithmic, -- check if the given vector fields are
    logarithmic

