isFreeDivisor -- check if the provided information is associated with a free divisor
************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        t=isFreeDivisor(M)
        t=isFreeDivisor(m)
        t=isFreeDivisor(f)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, of vector fields, usually
        square
      * m, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, of vector fields
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a polynomial
        defining a hypersurface
  * Outputs:
      * t, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether M or m
        generate the module of vector fields for a free divisor, or whether f=0
        defines a free divisor

Description
===========

Determine whether the given object is associated to a free divisor, using a
variety of methods. A free divisor is a hypersurface germ $X$ for which the
associated module of logarithmic vector fields (see *note derlog: derlog,) is
free.

When given a *note RingElement: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement, f, this tests
whether f=0 is a free divisor by computing derlog(ideal (f)) and then testing
if this is a free module by computing a partial *note freeResolution:
(Complexes)freeResolution,. This method may give false negatives if the
resolution computed is not minimal; use with caution.

When given a *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, M, this tests whether the
given vector fields are a free set of generators of the module of logarithmic
vector fields for a free divisor. A criterion of Kyoji Saito is used: if the
number of vector fields provided equals the dimension of the ambient space
(i.e., M is square), the vector fields generate a Lie algebra, and the
determinant of the matrix is reduced (square-free), then the provided vector
fields are a free basis of the free module derlog(ideal det(M)), and det(M)=0
defines a free divisor. This method may give false negatives if redundant
generators are provided.

When given a *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, this tests whether the module
is the module of logarithmic vector fields of a free divisor. The method
applies the *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, version of the command to the
generators given by gens(m). If the generators provided by *note generators:
(Macaulay2Doc)generators, are not minimal, then this may give false negatives;
use *note trim: (Macaulay2Doc)trim, first.

For example, this is not a free divisor:

+------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[a,b,c];             |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : f=a*c-b^2;               |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : M=derlog(ideal (f))      |
|                              |
|o3 = image | 2b a  0  0  |    |
|           | c  0  b  a  |    |
|           | 0  -c 2c 2b |    |
|                              |
|                             3|
|o3 : R-module, submodule of R |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : isFreeDivisor(gens M)    |
|                              |
|o4 = false                    |
+------------------------------+
|i5 : isFreeDivisor(M)         |
|                              |
|o5 = false                    |
+------------------------------+
|i6 : isFreeDivisor(f)         |
|                              |
|o6 = false                    |
+------------------------------+



This is a free divisor:

+------------------------------+
|i7 : f=a*(a*c-b^2);           |
+------------------------------+
|i8 : M=derlog(ideal (f))      |
|                              |
|o8 = image | a  0  0  |       |
|           | 0  b  a  |       |
|           | -c 2c 2b |       |
|                              |
|                             3|
|o8 : R-module, submodule of R |
+------------------------------+
|i9 : isFreeDivisor(gens M)    |
|                              |
|o9 = true                     |
+------------------------------+
|i10 : isFreeDivisor(M)        |
|                              |
|o10 = true                    |
+------------------------------+
|i11 : isFreeDivisor(f)        |
|                              |
|o11 = true                    |
+------------------------------+



This is a free divisor:

+-------------------------------+
|i12 : f=a;                     |
+-------------------------------+
|i13 : D=derlog(ideal (f))      |
|                               |
|o13 = image | 0 0 a |          |
|            | 1 0 0 |          |
|            | 0 1 0 |          |
|                               |
|                              3|
|o13 : R-module, submodule of R |
+-------------------------------+
|i14 : isFreeDivisor(f)         |
|                               |
|o14 = true                     |
+-------------------------------+
|i15 : isFreeDivisor(D)         |
|                               |
|o15 = true                     |
+-------------------------------+

but the vector fields in M are not a generating set of the logarithmic vector
fields:

+-----------------------------------------+
|i16 : M=matrix {{a,0,0},{0,a,0},{0,0,1}};|
|                                         |
|              3      3                   |
|o16 : Matrix R  <-- R                    |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i17 : isSubset(image M,D)                |
|                                         |
|o17 = true                               |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i18 : isFreeDivisor(M)                   |
|                                         |
|o18 = false                              |
+-----------------------------------------+



False negatives can occur with a set of generators that is not minimal:

+--------------------------------------------+
|i19 : isFreeDivisor((gens D)|M)             |
|                                            |
|o19 = false                                 |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i20 : isFreeDivisor(trim image ((gens D)|M))|
|                                            |
|o20 = true                                  |
+--------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note VectorFields: Top, -- vector fields
  * *note isLieAlgebra: isLieAlgebra, -- check that a module of vector fields
    is closed under the Lie bracket
  * *note derlog: derlog, -- compute the logarithmic (tangent) vector fields to
    an ideal

Ways to use isFreeDivisor:
==========================

  * "isFreeDivisor(Matrix)"
  * "isFreeDivisor(Module)"
  * "isFreeDivisor(RingElement)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note isFreeDivisor: isFreeDivisor, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

