isVectorField -- test whether a module or matrix can be interpreted as a collection of vector fields
****************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        b=isVectorField(m)
        b=isVectorField(M)
  * Inputs:
      * m, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the provided
        module or matrix can be interpreted as a collection of vector fields

Description
===========

This determines whether the provided *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, or
*note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, can be interpreted as a collection of
vector fields.

For a *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module, to be interpreted as a module of
vector fields, the module must be presented as a submodule of a free module
whose rank equals the number of variables in the ring.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y];                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : isVectorField(image matrix {{x,y^2}})      |
|                                                |
|o2 = false                                      |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isVectorField(image matrix {{x,y^2},{0,0}})|
|                                                |
|o3 = true                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+



For a *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, it must have the correct number of
rows.

+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isVectorField(matrix {{x,y^2}})      |
|                                          |
|o4 = false                                |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isVectorField(matrix {{x,y^2},{0,0}})|
|                                          |
|o5 = true                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Despite the name, the function does not check the number of vector fields
provided.

See also
========

  * *note VectorFields: Top, -- vector fields

Ways to use isVectorField:
==========================

  * "isVectorField(Matrix)"
  * "isVectorField(Module)"

